# PATCH: 018-custom-newtab
#
# Replaces the new-tab page with a self-contained DenBrowser shortcuts page.
#
# Rationale: this browser runs in permanent private browsing with extensions
# locked down, so the activity-stream new-tab page never renders — its built-in
# add-on's background script does not run, so about:newtab is left blank/stuck.
# We serve our own static page instead.
#
# Mechanism:
#   1. about:denbrowserhome is registered as a plain chrome about: page via the
#      C++ AboutRedirector (AboutRedirector.cpp + components.conf), exactly like
#      about:robots and about:privatebrowsing. It maps to
#      chrome://browser/content/denbrowser-newtab.{html,css} (registered in
#      browser/base/jar.mn). Flags are URI_SAFE_FOR_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT |
#      URI_MUST_LOAD_IN_CHILD: the page renders as untrusted content in a normal
#      child content process — it deliberately avoids the privileged-about
#      process and ALLOW_SCRIPT (the page is static, no JS). This sidesteps the
#      newtab built-in add-on entirely, along with its init handshake.
#   2. AboutNewTab.newTabURL is pinned to about:denbrowserhome, so every new tab
#      (the "+" button, Ctrl+T, preloading — all of which resolve through
#      BROWSER_NEW_TAB_URL → AboutNewTab.newTabURL) loads our page. The
#      permanent-PBM logic in BROWSER_NEW_TAB_URL passes our about: URL through
#      unchanged (it is not a moz-extension URL and the new tab is not
#      extension-controlled). about:newtab itself is left untouched.
#   3. about:denbrowserhome is added to gInitialPages so it is treated as an
#      initial page (blank URL bar, etc.) like about:newtab.
#
#   The tiles between the page's DEN_SHORTCUTS markers are generated at build
#   time by build.sh (Step 2.7) from config/site-config.json's "bookmarks".
#   The page is pure static HTML (no script), so clicking a tile is an ordinary
#   top-level navigation.

